{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["And the meaning of זולות is contempt, like יקר מזולל, כי הייתי זוללה, כל מכבדיה הזילוה. And it lacks [a letter] where one is expected." "כרום — men of contempt, in the manner of וגבורתך במלחמה (and your might in battle), אל תהי מרי (be not myrrh?), ואני תפלה (and I am prayer). And some say: from זולל וסובא (glutton and drunkard). And the first is correct."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {1 "The phrases 'אל תהי מרי' and 'ואני תפלה' appear to be cited as lexical parallels for the construct-type usage, but the reference is obscure and possibly corrupt; rendered hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:27:13.445653405Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}